::: {.doc-subject}

Make a validation step that checks the length of text in tokens.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/pointblank/blob/main/pointblank/text.py#L428-L528){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
text.token_length(
    column,
    tokenizer,
    min_val=None,
    max_val=None,
    na_pass=False,
    cache=True,
    pre=None,
    segments=None,
    thresholds=None,
    actions=None,
    brief=None,
    active=True,
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

A language model reads text as tokens, and most have a limit on how many they can take in, so
the documents of a corpus for training (or a set of prompts) need to be neither too short nor
too long, in the tokens of the model's tokenizer. The step is a
`~~pointblank.Validate.col_vals_scored()` step with a
[`token_count()`](`pointblank.scorers.token_count`) scorer, and a row fails if its number of
tokens is below `min_val=` or above `max_val=`.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[column]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The column with the text.

<code>[tokenizer]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The tokenizer: the name of a Hugging Face tokenizer, `"tiktoken:"` and the name of an
    encoding or a model, `"whitespace"`, a tokenizer object, or a function (see
    [`token_count()`](`pointblank.scorers.token_count`)).

<code>[min_val]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The fewest and the most tokens that a text can have (at least one of them is needed).

<code>[max_val]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The fewest and the most tokens that a text can have (at least one of them is needed).

<code>[na_pass]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Whether a row with a missing value passes.

<code>[cache]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Where the counts are kept: in memory (`True`), in a directory, or not at all (`False`).

<code>[pre]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Callable | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   A function that transforms the table before the step, as in the validation methods.

<code>[segments]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [SegmentSpec | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The segments of the step, as in the validation methods.

<code>[thresholds]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | float | bool | tuple | dict | Thresholds | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The thresholds of the step (by default, those of the validation).

<code>[actions]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Actions | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The actions of the step.

<code>[brief]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   A brief for the step.

<code>[active]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | Callable]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Whether the step is active.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Steps]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The step, to be added to a validation with
    [`Validate.add_steps()`](`pointblank.Validate.add_steps`).
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}



A real check would use the tokenizer of a model (e.g., `"tiktoken:cl100k_base"`). Here, the
tokens are the words, split on whitespace.

::: {#212cdc41 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pointblank as pb
import polars as pl

prompts = pl.DataFrame(
    {"prompt": ["Summarize the article in two sentences.", "Hi", "List three uses of salt."]}
)

(
    pb.Validate(data=prompts)
    .add_steps(pb.text.token_length("prompt", tokenizer="whitespace", min_val=3))
    .interrogate()
)
```

